But that's the only way you could exist. If-- you have to keep on going. I mean, it's nothing you can change. You can-- you can't forget your past. But you have to live in the future. I mean, it's nothing that--

INT: Would you consider yourself optimistic about life?

LR: Yes. Yes, it's-- you have to-- you have to-- you have to-- you have to try, and life is too short to be nice. And to believe in your religion-- never-- never be ashamed of your religion. Because six million people were killed with their religion.

Not it's because they were criminals, just because they were born Jewish. That were only crime they had. So you should never be ashamed to be of your religion.

INT: Do you support the State of Israel?

LR: Yes, I do. Buy Israeli bonds. I should go to Israel more. I was only once.

But thank God, from all this bad come out a State of Israel. Because the newcomers, they went. You know, they didn't have where to go. So thank God for Truman, that he OKed the State of Israel. And you know?

So we have a country with all-- with all different nationalities. We could say we could be proud. A Jew couldn't done nothing in Europe.

How you fight, like my father? He was-- he had two stars. He would-- he had-- he had medals for bravery. But when the-- when it came, he was a dirty Jew, he fought for what?

In Israel, the world cannot take it, that-- the-- it-- the-- what they done to the country, to the desert is blooming. And-- and-- and what they could do, that the Jew could be just beaten. But he cannot do it back.

He cannot fight back in the-- in the-- in the Europe, the non-Jews were-- were-- you know, would hit the Jew, the Jew run away. They were afraid. They were afraid.

But they see that a Jew could do-- and you know, the Jew did so much for humanity. And they, all the time, put the Jew down, all the time. All the world want to put the Jew down.

